ng is added for you, and what you write keeps the order you wrote it in. `children` also accepts a function for picker state"},"380":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-23","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#features","content":"**Trigger and calendar**: An empty `Button slot=\"trigger\"` renders a calendar icon and the formatted value from the field. `DatePickerCalendar` (and `DateRangePickerCalendar`) is the calendar in the popover it opens: it takes `Calendar` props plus `popoverProps` for the overlay. Write `Popover`, `Content`, and `Calendar` yourself to replace the whole overlay"},"381":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-24","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#features","content":"**Sizes**: Each picker is a `SizeProvider`. `size` (`sm`, `md`, `lg`) sets its label, trigger, description, error, and the calendar it opens; without it, the picker follows the surrounding scope"},"382":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-25","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#features","content":"`DatePicker` (single) and `DateRangePicker` (range): a read-only formatted date label; the whole field opens a calendar popover"},"383":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-26","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#features","content":"Built on React Aria - native form integration, validation, focus management, and screen-reader support"},"384":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-27","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#features","content":"Label formatting via `formatOptions` / `placeholder` on the picker itself, or on `DatePickerValue` / `DateRangePickerValue` in a trigger you write"},"385":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-28","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#features","content":"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"},"386":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-29","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#working-with-dates","content":"Values are `CalendarDate` objects. Import the date primitives you need from the `@godaddy/antares/date` subpath:"},"387":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-30","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#working-with-dates","content":"Import date helpers from `@godaddy/antares/date` (a re-export of\n`@internationalized/date`).\nWrap the app in `<I18nProvider>` so formatting and the calendar follow the user's locale."},"388":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-31","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#default","content":"A single date picker with a `Label`."},"389":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-32","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#range","content":"A start/end range picker."},"390":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-33","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#controlled","content":"Driving the value with `useState`."},"391":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-34","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#format-options","content":"Controlling the trigger's label format via `formatOptions`."},"392":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-35","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#min--max","content":"Bounding selectable dates with `minValue` / `maxValue`."},"393":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-36","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#with-error","content":"An invalid picker showing a validation message via `isInvalid` and a `FieldError`."},"394":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-37","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#disabled","content":"A disabled picker via `isDisabled`."},"395":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-38","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#composed","content":"Write the trigger and the overlay yourself instead of composing `DatePickerCalendar`, for full\ncontrol over the popover and the calendar."},"396":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-39","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#composed-range","content":"Write a DateRangePicker's trigger and overlay from lower-level pieces the same way."},"397":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-40","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#sizes","content":"`size` sets the label, trigger, and calendar. Without it, the picker follows the surrounding\nsize scope."},"398":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"page","content":"DropZone","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone"},"399":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-0","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone","content":"A standalone region that accepts drag-and-drop file interactions, rendering a clearly defined target area where users can drop files."},"400":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-1","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#installation","content":"Installation"},"401":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-2","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#examples","content":"Examples"},"402":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-3","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#default","content":"Default"},"403":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-4","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#disabled","content":"Disabled"},"404":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-5","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#file-upload","content":"File Upload"},"405":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-6","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#drop-target-label","content":"Drop Target Label"},"406":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-7","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#replace-existing-file","content":"Replace Existing File"},"407":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-8","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"408":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-9","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#keyboard","content":"Keyboard"},"409":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-10","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#screen-readers","content":"Screen readers"},"410":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-11","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"411":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-12","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#props","content":"Props"},"412":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-13","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#dropzone","content":"DropZone"},"413":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-14","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#default","content":"A minimal drop zone. The `onDrop` callback receives the dropped items; use the exported `isFileDropItem` guard to narrow them to files. Wrap the instructional text in `<Text slot=\"label\">` so it labels the visually hidden drop button for screen readers."},"414":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-15","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#disabled","content":"Set `isDisabled` to prevent the drop zone from accepting interactions. The zone is dimmed and the cursor indicates it is not interactive."},"415":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-16","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#file-upload","content":"A reference composition combining `DropZone` with `FileTrigger` to support both click-to-browse and drag-and-drop. Use this as a starting point and adapt the accepted formats, size limit, and handlers to your product's requirements."},"416":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-17","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#drop-target-label","content":"Pass a render-prop function as `children` to change the zone's content while a valid drag is active. Branching on `isDropTarget` requires no extra state. Pair it with `getDropOperation` to reject unsupported types - the label only appears when the drag is accepted."},"417":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-18","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#replace-existing-file","content":"Use `children` as a render function to show different content based on the current zone state - here, swapping the default label for \"Drop to replace\" when a file is already selected and a new drag is active. The same `onDrop` handler services both the drag path and the `FileTrigger` click path, so either gesture replaces the selection."},"418":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-19","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#keyboard","content":"Key"},"419":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-20","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#keyboard","content":"Description"},"420":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-21","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#keyboard","content":"`Tab`"},"421":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-22","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#keyboard","content":"Moves focus to the drop zone"},"422":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-23","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#keyboard","content":"`Enter` / `Space`"},"423":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-24","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#keyboard","content":"Opens the file picker so files can be selected without a pointer"},"424":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-25","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#screen-readers","content":"The drop zone renders a visually hidden `<button>` inside the container. Assistive technology discovers and announces this button as an interactive element — activating it opens the native file picker without a pointer."},"425":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-26","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#screen-readers","content":"The button's accessible name is built from two sources, combined in order:"},"426":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-27","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#screen-readers","content":"**`<Text slot=\"label\">`** — any `Text` child with `slot=\"label\"` has its `id` linked to the button via `aria-labelledby`. This is the recommended way to provide a contextual label that is also visible to sighted users."},"427":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-28","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#screen-readers","content":"**`aria-label`** — pass `aria-label` on the `DropZone` component to override or supplement the label (e.g. `aria-label=\"Upload profile photo\"`). When no `Text slot=\"label\"` is present and no `aria-label` is set, the button falls back to the default \"DropZone\" label provided by React Aria."},"428":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-29","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#best-practices","content":"Use the drop zone alongside a button-based file picker — drag-and-drop is a convenience, never the only way to upload."},"429":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-30","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#best-practices","content":"Replace the default text with `children` to communicate the accepted file types and size limits up front."},"430":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-31","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#best-practices","content":"Let the drop zone fill its container; constrain it with the surrounding layout rather than setting a fixed width on the component itself."},"431":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-32","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#best-practices","content":"Reflect upload state (validating, uploading, error) outside the drop zone so the target area stays clear and predictable."},"432":{"id":"/docs/components/drawer","page_id":"/docs/components/drawer","type":"page","content":"Drawer","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drawer"},"433":{"id":"/docs/components/drawer-0","page_id":"/docs/components/drawer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drawer","content":"An overlay panel that slides in from a screen edge, supporting sidebar navigation and bottom sheets."},"434":{"id":"/docs/components/drawer-1","page_id":"/docs/components/drawer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drawer#installation","content":"Installation"},"435":{"id":"/docs/components/drawer-2","page_id":"/docs/components/drawer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drawer#examples","content":"Examples"},"436":{"id":"/docs/components/drawer-3","page_id":"/docs/components/drawer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drawer#default","content":"Default"},"437":{"id":"/docs/components/drawer-4","page_id":"/docs/components/drawer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drawer#bottom-sheet","content":"Bottom Sheet"},"438":{"id":"/docs/components/drawer-5","page_id":"/docs/components/drawer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drawer#placements","content":"Placements"},"439":{"id":"/docs/components/drawer-6","page_id":"/docs/components/drawer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drawer#nested-popover","content":"Nested Popover"},"440":{"id":"/docs/components/drawer-7","page_id":"/docs/components/drawer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drawer#no-escape-dismiss","content":"No Escape Dismiss"},"441":{"id":"/docs/components/drawer-8","page_id":"/docs/components/drawer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drawer#scrollable-content","content":"Scrollable content"},"442":{"id":"/docs/components/drawer-9","page_id":"/docs/components/drawer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drawer#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"443":{"id":"/docs/components/drawer-10","page_id":"/docs/components/drawer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drawer#keyboard","content":"Keyboard"},"444":{"id":"/docs/components/drawer-11","page_id":"/docs/components/drawer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drawer#aria","content":"ARIA"},"445":{"id":"/docs/components/drawer-12","page_id":"/docs/components/drawer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drawer#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"446":{"id":"/docs/components/drawer-13","page_id":"/docs/components/drawer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drawer#props","content":"Props"},"447":{"id":"/docs/components/drawer-14","page_id":"/docs/components/drawer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drawer#drawer","content":"Drawer"},"448":{"id":"/docs/components/drawer-15","page_id":"/docs/components/drawer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drawer#drawertrigger","content":"DrawerTrigger"},"449":{"id":"/docs/components/drawer-16","page_id":"/docs/components/drawer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drawer","content":"An overlay panel that slides in from a screen edge. Built on the same RAC stack as `Modal` (a\nmodal overlay with an `elevation=\"overlay\"` panel and CSS transitions), it supports sidebar\nnavigation and bottom sheets."},"450":{"id":"/docs/components/drawer-17","page_id":"/docs/components/drawer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drawer","content":"`DrawerTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Drawer>`, handling open\nstate automatically."},"451":{"id":"/docs/components/drawer-18","page_id":"/docs/components/drawer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drawer#default","content":"Use `<DrawerTrigger>` to wrap a trigger button and a `<Drawer>`. The drawer opens when the trigger is pressed."},"452":{"id":"/docs/components/drawer-19","page_id":"/docs/components/drawer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drawer#bottom-sheet","content":"Use `placement=\"bottom\"` with controlled state for a bottom sheet pattern