 those bars — so a single series can carry a different color\nper category. All three periods here share the same category-to-color map, so each\nchannel keeps one color across every period; the comparison periods are dropped to\nreduced opacity."],[233,"`CheckboxGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Checkbox` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Checkbox` takes label text next to the indicator."],[326,"`ChipButton` for menu filters and other actions with a Chip-like appearance"],[344,"`ChipButton` is a real button and exposes menu state through `MenuTrigger`; provide an accessible name when the visible content is incomplete."],[322,"`ChipGroup` + `ChipList` + `Chip` for grouped values, selection, keyboard navigation, and removal"],[337,"`ChipGroup` owns selection and removal behavior. Use a Chip render prop for\nstate-dependent content, and `Button` with `slot=\"remove\"` together with\n`onRemove` for removable items. See **Toggle Chips** and **Removable Chips**."],[1666,"`className` and `style` apply to the tooltip panel."],[1886,"`colorIndex` pins each series to a palette color. Any series can use any index,\nindependently — here two pairs each share an index so an actual line and its\ndashed forecast read as the same color, distinguished only by line style."],[1005,"`currentStep` is the single source of truth for the timeline. Omit it for a not-yet-started flow where every step is `future`; pass the step count for a fully completed flow where every step is `past`."],[568,"`data-color`: Applied when color prop is set"],[571,"`data-flip`: Applied when flip prop is set (\"horizontal\" or \"vertical\")"],[567,"`data-icon`: The icon name (always present)"],[569,"`data-loading`: Applied during icon loading from CDN"],[570,"`data-mode`: Applied when mode prop is set (e.g., \"sprite\")"],[572,"`data-rotate`: Applied when rotate prop is set (90, 180, or 270)"],[1372,"`data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focused`, `data-focus-visible`, `data-disabled`, `data-readonly`, `data-invalid`, `data-required`, `data-size`"],[382,"`DatePicker` (single) and `DateRangePicker` (range): a read-only formatted date label; the whole field opens a calendar popover"],[1478,"`Detail` is supporting copy, such as captions and metadata, on the detail ramp. It keeps the\nsurrounding color; add `emphasis=\"passive\"` to mute it."],[450,"`DrawerTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Drawer>`, handling open\nstate automatically."],[489,"`emphasis` picks a feedback color and changes only the color."],[1469,"`emphasis` picks a feedback color and changes only the color."],[1477,"`emphasis` selects a feedback color and changes nothing else. Without it, text inherits the\nsurrounding color."],[885,"`Enter/Space`"],[422,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[662,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[459,"`Escape`"],[811,"`Escape`"],[887,"`Escape`"],[1671,"`Escape`"],[730,"`FileTrigger` adds no visuals or ARIA of its own — accessibility comes from the pressable child you provide. Use a component with an accessible name (e.g. an Antares `Button` with clear label text) so assistive technology announces the action. The underlying `<input>` is visually hidden but remains operable by keyboard through the child's press behavior."],[1955,"`Flex` is a one-dimensional layout component for arranging children in rows or columns with alignment and spacing control. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[576,"`focusable=\"false\"`: Prevents keyboard focus"],[1993,"`Grid` is a two-dimensional CSS Grid layout component for complex grid-based layouts. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[491,"`Heading` renders a semantic `h1`-`h6` element via the `level` prop.\nInside a `Modal`/`Dialog`, add `slot=\"title\"` and it labels the dialog automatically."],[650,"`InlineDrawerPanel` is the collapsible content for the accordion pattern — a thin wrapper over RAC `DisclosurePanel` that hides when collapsed. The trigger is any component you slot in with `slot=\"trigger\"` — there's no dedicated trigger component."],[679,"`Input` is the single-line control inside a field, not a field on its own. Prefer `TextField` or `NumberField` as the parent; see those components for fuller examples."],[1869,"`legendPosition` puts the legend above or below the plot, or hides it with `null`. Multi-series charts get a bottom legend by default."],[492,"`level` sets the semantics and `size` sets the look, so the two never have to match. Without\n`size`, a heading takes the size scope's heading tier at any level."],[1924,"`lg` - Large spacing"],[709,"`ListBox` requires either `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. For a labeled, popover-style picker, prefer `Select`."],[1923,"`md` - Medium spacing"],[765,"`MenuTrigger` exposes its open state via `isOpen`/`onOpenChange`,\nwhich can be used to drive the rotation of a chevron icon."],[151,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[385,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[804,"`Modal` accepts `isOpen` and `onOpenChange` directly, so it can be controlled without a\n`ModalTrigger`. Useful when the modal is opened from several places at once."],[799,"`ModalTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Modal>`, handling open state automatically. Based on RAC `DialogTrigger`."],[1004,"`orientation` switches between `horizontal` (accent bar on top) and `vertical` (accent bar on the leading edge)."],[1721,"`orientation=\"horizontal\"` swaps the axes: categories run down the side and values across the bottom. Reach for it when the labels are long or the chart is really a ranking."],[1319,"`overflowLabels` is optional and defaults to \"Previous tabs\" and \"Next tabs\". Provide localized labels when needed; they should describe the logical direction rather than physical directions like \"left\" or \"right\", as the component automatically handles RTL layouts."],[1661,"`overlay` elevation panel positioned relative to its trigger, with an optional arrow"],[670,"`placement` does not flip in RTL; the side is decided by document/flex order."],[653,"`placement` selects the collapse axis (`left`/`right` → width, `top`/`bottom` → height)"],[879,"`PopoverTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Popover>`, handling open state and positioning automatically.\nBased on RAC `DialogTrigger`. To anchor a popover to an element it doesn't wrap, pass `triggerRef` instead."],[656,"`prefers-reduced-motion` support"],[913,"`Pressable` accepts the React Aria press props, including `onPress`, `onPressStart`, `onPressEnd`, `onPressUp`, and `onPressChange`."],[918,"`Pressable` automatically applies React Aria state attributes such as `[data-hovered]`, `[data-pressed]`, `[data-focus-visible]`, and `[data-disabled]` to the child. Ensure the child component styles these states appropriately if it overrides the default `Pressable` styles."],[1059,"`RadioGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Radio` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Radio` takes label text next to the indicator. `orientation` also sets keyboard-navigation direction and ARIA."],[1888,"`renderTooltip` example combining a pair of series. Each pair shares a `colorIndex`\n(solid actual + dashed forecast); hovering either line shows the percent change of\nthe forecast against the actual for that pair, wrapped in the default styled popover."],[1889,"`renderTooltip` example styled as a period-over-period comparison card. Paired series\n(solid current period + dashed previous period) share a `colorIndex`; hovering either\nline shows both dated values and the percent change, wrapped in the default popover."],[1887,"`renderTooltip` lets you render a fully custom tooltip and know which curve is\nhovered. Paired series share a `colorIndex`; hovering either line shows a\ntooltip specific to that line, wrapped in the default styled popover."],[813,"`role=\"dialog\"` is applied automatically by the underlying React Aria `Dialog`"],[889,"`role=\"dialog\"` is applied automatically by the underlying React Aria `Dialog`"],[463,"`role=\"dialog\"` with `aria-modal=\"true\"` on the drawer panel (via RAC Modal)"],[575,"`role=\"img\"`: When title prop is provided"],[574,"`role=\"presentation\"`: For decorative icons"],[283,"`role=\"progressbar\"` on the container"],[967,"`role=\"progressbar\"` on the container"],[1069,"`role=\"radio\"` on each option"],[1194,"`role=\"radio\"` on each segment"],[1068,"`role=\"radiogroup\"` on the container"],[1193,"`role=\"radiogroup\"` on the container"],[1591,"`selectionMode=\"multiple\"` → `role=\"toolbar\"` on container, `role=\"button\"` + `aria-pressed` per item"],[1590,"`selectionMode=\"single\"` → `role=\"radiogroup\"` on container, `role=\"radio\"` + `aria-checked` per item"],[771,"`size` controls item density. Shown here as two standalone menus so both\nsizes are visible at once; in practice you set `size` on the `Menu` inside a\n`MenuTrigger`."],[1468,"`size` picks a step on the component's own ramp (`xs` to `2xl`) and changes only the font size."],[1511,"`size` sets every part, each on its own role ramp. Without it, the lockup follows the size\nscope."],[847,"`size` sets the label, input, and steppers. Without it, the field follows the surrounding size\nscope."],[1641,"`size` sets the label, input, description, and any control composed inside. Without it, the\nfield follows the surrounding size scope."],[397,"`size` sets the label, trigger, and calendar. Without it, the picker follows the surrounding\nsize scope."],[805,"`size` sets the modal's text, controls, and spacing. Without it, the modal follows the size\nscope around its trigger."],[490,"`slot=\"title\"` inside a `Modal` or `Dialog` sets the accessible name, and takes the overlay's\ntitle tier, one step above the heading tier."],[1922,"`sm` - Small spacing"],[1215,"`sm`, `md`, or `lg` for the adopted components inside (listed below): their text, controls, and\ndefault spacing."],[90,"`Space` / `Enter`"],[1398,"`Space` toggles the switch when it has focus"],[1006,"`status` is independent of timeline and only controls the status icon and (for `error`) the accent bar color."],[88,"`Tab`"],[420,"`Tab`"],[461,"`Tab`"],[664,"`Tab`"],[809,"`Tab`"],[1669,"`Tab`"],[1323,"`Tab`: `data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focus-visible`, and `data-disabled`."],[1320,"`TabList` must be rendered inside `Tabs` and must provide `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. Give each `Tab` and its corresponding `TabPanel` the same `id`; React Aria uses that key to build their accessible relationship."],[1324,"`TabPanel`: `data-inert` when a force-mounted inactive panel is not interactive."],[1322,"`Tabs`: `data-design=\"underline\"` or `data-design=\"manilla\"`."],[1466,"`Text` applies the body role and `Detail` the detail role, each at the tier of the nearest\n`SizeProvider`, or `md` outside any scope."],[1465,"`Text` is body copy and `Detail` is supporting copy: captions, metadata, and hints."],[1486,"`TextArea` is the multiline control inside a field, not a field on its own. Prefer `TextField` as the parent; see that component for fuller examples."],[1516,"`TextLockup` positions and type-sets its parts; you supply them. That means anything else can\nsit alongside them — a call to action, a second paragraph, an image — without the component\ngrowing a prop for it."],[1126,"`thumbNames` configures native form field names and does not provide accessible labels. Likewise, `valueLabel`, `minLabel`, and `maxLabel` are visual context rather than substitutes for accessible naming."],[949,"`titleInfo` requires `title` to be set — the info icon is contextually tied to the title label. If `title` is absent, `titleInfo` has no effect."],[1660,"`TooltipTrigger` wraps a focusable element and a `<Tooltip>`, handling hover/focus state and positioning automatically."],[1880,"`tooltipValueFormatter` shapes only the tooltip values, so you can show full currency or units there while the axis stays compact."],[950,"`trend` is intended to accompany `description` to provide temporal context (e.g. \"↑ +3% vs. last month\"). A trend icon alone, with no description, leaves the direction unanchored (\"up since *when*?\"). If `description` is not provided, `trend` has no effect."],[1890,"`variant` sets each series' line style — 'solid' (default), 'dashed', or\n'dotted' — useful for distinguishing actuals from forecasts or targets. The\nlegend swatch mirrors each line's style."],[1868,"`xBaseline` and `yBaseline` control the main axis lines themselves. Dropping them gives a lighter, more editorial chart."],[1723,"`xDomain` and `yDomain` pin down exactly which categories and value range to draw. Here category `F` has no data and still gets an empty slot, and the Y range stays `[0, 40]` even though the largest bar is 30 - handy when several charts need to share a scale."],[1873,"`xDomain` and `yDomain` pin the visible range. Use them to keep a fixed scale, or to keep several charts comparable."],[1864,"`xGridlines` and `yGridlines` add faint lines across the plot so it is easier to read a value back off an axis."],[1925,"`xl` - Extra large spacing"],[1866,"`xLabels` and `yLabels` toggle the tick labels on each axis. Turn them off for sparklines or when the surrounding UI already names the values."],[1874,"`xNice` and `yNice` round the domain out to friendlier numbers (e.g. 0.2 to 1.0), so ticks land on values people e